From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:25:53 +0800
Subject: HID: nanosic: reject unsupported HID report requests

The MCU has no transport for HID feature and output reports. Return
EOPNOTSUPP when asked for either, and suppress the touchpad feature
queries after HID core has set the initial quirks. Input mapping
can use the limits already provided by the descriptor.

Link: https://github.com/slwyts/Project-SunUEFI/commit/b5949f98afb60a23287052de5c3532a0567c2975
Signed-off-by: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
---
 drivers/hid/hid-nanosic-wn8030.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/hid/hid-nanosic-wn8030.c b/drivers/hid/hid-nanosic-wn8030.c
index 86ed4059e9aa250b740574afdf7bb4f385a9cd48..cff071e485d0ab9807d6191b9da53540dbe3df39 100644
--- a/drivers/hid/hid-nanosic-wn8030.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/hid-nanosic-wn8030.c
@@ -615,6 +615,10 @@ static int nanosic_wn8030_hid_parse(struct hid_device *hid)
 
 static int nanosic_wn8030_hid_start(struct hid_device *hid)
 {
+	/* HID core resets quirks before probe; set this before input mapping. */
+	if (hid->product == 0x00A1)
+		hid->quirks |= HID_QUIRK_NO_INIT_REPORTS;
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
@@ -637,7 +641,8 @@ static int nanosic_wn8030_raw_request(struct hid_device *hid,
 				      __u8 *buf, size_t len,
 				      unsigned char rtype, int reqtype)
 {
-	return len;
+	/* The MCU protocol has no HID feature/output report transport. */
+	return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 }
 
 static inline u32 nanosic_wn8030_checksum32(const u8 *data, int size)
